      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•Charming end-of-terrace period home with uninterrupted views across Baldoyle Bay towards Portmarnock Point and Sutton Golf Club\r\n\r\n•Located beside a designated Special Area of Conservation and Special Protection Area, renowned for its coastal scenery and birdlife\r\n\r\n•Spectacular east-facing sunrise views from the front of the property\r\n\r\n•Private gravel driveway to the front with shared side pedestrian access to the rear garden\r\n\r\n•Sunny south-west facing walled patio garden ideal for outdoor dining and entertaining\r\n\r\n•Bright open-plan kitchen and dining area with direct access to the rear patio\r\n\r\n•Cosy front living room featuring stunning bay views and an attractive iron fireplace\r\n\r\n•Two spacious upstairs bedrooms along with a well-appointed family bathroom\r\n\r\n•Lovingly maintained family home retaining its original charm and character throughout\r\n\r\n•Excellent location within walking distance of Baldoyle Village, Sutton Cross and Sutton DART Station, with scenic coastal walks towards Howth and Portmarnock nearby"
